; The hand-drawn room's creatures — a test fixture with frozen numbers.
;
; Deliberately NOT the game's own units. The hand-drawn room exists to answer
; "can the engine be played?", and it can only answer that if it stays still: were
; it built from the game's balance, every tuning pass would quietly change the
; world those tests run in, and a failure would mean "the hero is weaker now"
; rather than "the engine broke".
;
; So these numbers are fixed forever, and the skeletons carry no behaviour script:
; what this room exercises is the engine's own mechanics, with nothing layered on
; top. The skeletons keep a locomotor at zero speed because to the engine a shaped
; thing that cannot move is scenery and gets baked into the navigation grid — they
; would become walls, and the hero could never reach them.

Object
  Name = Rogue
  DisplayName = Hero
  KindOf = [INFANTRY, SELECTABLE, CAN_ATTACK]
  Cylinder
    Radius = 4
    Height = 12
  End
  VisionRange = 600
  ActiveBody
    MaxHealth = 200
  End
  MoveUpdate
    Speed = 45
    TurnRate = 720
  End
  WeaponUpdate
    Damage = 14
    AttackRange = 8
    ReloadFrames = 15
  End
End

Object
  Name = Skeleton
  DisplayName = Skeleton
  KindOf = [INFANTRY, SELECTABLE, CAN_ATTACK]
  Cylinder
    Radius = 4
    Height = 12
  End
  VisionRange = 90
  ActiveBody
    MaxHealth = 60
  End
  MoveUpdate
    Speed = 0
  End
  WeaponUpdate
    Damage = 4
    AttackRange = 10
    ReloadFrames = 30
  End
End
